      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_launcher_1a725a3958001b044eb14d96569b77f115" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int Launcher::run</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>run</name>
        <qualifiedname>Launcher::run</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Starts the target and returns its exit code. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Windows creates the target suspended, sends its process ID, and reads the reply. When the reply says didAttach, it waits for the target to exit. Otherwise it terminates the target. When the target cannot be created, it sends an error message. macOS opens the reply FIFO, sends the process ID of this process, and reads the reply. When the reply says didAttach, it closes the reply FIFO and replaces this process with the target. When execvp fails, it prints the error.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>The exit code of the target on Windows. failedLaunchExitCode when the target does not start or does not attach, and when execvp fails on macOS. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
